  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "selector",
      "note": "ServoSelector (extras/mmu/unit/selectors/mmu_servo_selector.py:75): `MMU_TYPE_LOW_RIDER_1_0` does `select SERVO_SELECTOR` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.low_rider:6) and trades the selector stepper for one RC servo -- `[mmu_unit unit0] selector_servo: unit0_selector_servo`, with no selector `[mmu_stepper]` section -- beside the gear stepper. The servo part is HH's `CHOICE_SERVO_TYPE` default `SERVO_TYPE_DM996` (Kconfig.low_rider:49-50), duration 0.6, dwell 1.0, always_active 0, bypass -1, release 0, max 180 degrees (Kconfig.low_rider:53-63); the type's `imply`s also give `filament_always_gripped: 1` and `variable_rotation_distances: 1` (Kconfig.low_rider:9-10). klipper-mmu drives it as a SERVO selector (`KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_KIND_SERVO`) on `KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_SERVO`, Klipper's scheduled software PWM on any GPIO: one angle per gate, seeded from the table below and replaced by angles saved with `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE_SELECTOR`, release angle 0 and a 1.0 s dwell, the same as Happy Hare. There is no selector axis to home. Software candidate: it builds and passes the simulators, but has not run on real hardware."
    },
    {
      "concept": "lane_count",
      "note": "6 gates: `PARAM_NUM_GATES` default 6 (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.low_rider:33), recorded as `device.gates: 6` and `[mmu_unit unit0] num_gates: 6`. The shipped angle table is written per gate count (Kconfig.low_rider:68-72), so the 6-gate default is the table below and nothing is rescaled."
    },
    {
      "concept": "gate_positions",
      "note": "Servo angles, one per gate, shipped but not calibrated: `PARAM_SERVO_GATE_ANGLES` default `30, 60, 90, 120, 150, 180` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.low_rider:67-72) -- gate 0 at 30 degrees, gate 5 at 180, with 0 reserved for the release position. The file's own comment: 'Reserve 0 degrees for the release position, then distribute gates evenly over the remaining selector travel up to 180 degrees'. The render carries the same table (`selector_servo` plus `servo_gate_angles`), and these are klipper-mmu's default gate angles (`KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_SERVO_GATE_ANGLES_DEG`) until angles measured with `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE_SELECTOR` replace them."
    },
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "Arrival is an extruder-mounted switch, and this profile wires none, so LOAD records the real failure: PRELOAD and LOAD both home onto `unit0:mmu_shared_exit` (the only switch the render declares, `mmu_shared_exit_switch_pin`), then LOAD runs `Homing filament to extruder endstop` on endstop `extruder` with `endstop_pos: 700` (layout `extruder` = 700) and never trips it -- the harness records `!! Endstop 'extruder' not found` and `Failed to reach extruder 'extruder' endstop after moving 0.0mm`, leaving `operations.load.end.tip = 682`, `filament_pos: 4`, `gate_status: 1`, with that error latched into UNLOAD and EJECT too. That is HH's configured arrival, not a harness defect: the type `imply MMU_HAS_SENSOR_EXTRUDER` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.low_rider:7) and the render sets `extruder_homing_endstop: extruder`, while this baseline profile declares `[mmu_toolhead default] extruder_switch_pin` empty. klipper-mmu does not fabricate the missing switch either: LOAD ends at a local toolhead switch or at FPS arrival, so a build wires one of the two."
    },
    {
      "concept": "preload_park",
      "note": "PRELOAD homes onto `unit0:mmu_shared_exit` (layout 10.0) and parks `gate_preload_parking_distance: -25` mm behind it: `operations.preload.end.tip = -15` (`end.offset = -25.0` behind the switch). Same -25 as Pico MMU; note ViViD parks forward +10 instead."
    },
    {
      "concept": "unload_park",
      "note": "UNLOAD fast-retracts down the bowden (682 -> 22), reverse-homes onto `unit0:mmu_shared_exit` (10.0) and parks `gate_parking_distance: -25` mm behind it: `operations.unload.end.tip = -15.000001`, `gate_status: 2`. The `errors` recorded here are the latched LOAD extruder-endstop failure, not this operation's own."
    },
    {
      "concept": "eject_extra",
      "note": "EJECT retracts `gate_final_eject_distance: 20` mm from the -15.000001 park to `operations.eject.end.tip = -35.000001` with no endstop (`homing: 0`) -- the same 20 mm as MMX, not ERCF's longer gate clear. Its recorded error is the latched LOAD failure."
    },
    {
      "concept": "harness_artifact",
      "note": "Harness artifacts. SELECT records 0 moves: a ServoSelector's swing is a servo command, not a gear move, so the angle table above is the record of selection and the filament model never exercises the servo (there is no selector `[mmu_stepper]` section for this type). `[mmu_sensors unit0]` declares only `mmu_shared_exit_switch_pin`, so the device's gate sensing is that single shared switch -- PRELOAD has no gate switch of its own, and the layout's `mmu_entry`/`mmu_exit` positions are the harness's 1-D path, not per-gate hardware."
    }
  ]
